   "en": "And now the first light was scattering itself fresh across the earth, as Dawn left Tithonus's saffron bed. As soon as the queen, from her watchtower, saw the light beginning to whiten, saw the fleet moving off under matched sails, and realised the shore and the harbour lay empty, without a single oarsman, she struck her lovely breast [again and again|33,34],",
